<p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>

<p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>

<p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;text-indent:36pt;"><i><span style="text-decoration: underline; ">Long-term Incentive Program (</span></i><span style="text-decoration: underline; ">&#8220;</span><i><span style="text-decoration: underline; ">LTIP</span></i><span style="text-decoration: underline; ">&#8221;</span><i><span style="text-decoration: underline; ">)</span></i><i>.</i> The Compensation Committee has been establishing a more structured process to grant equity awards. In 2025, restricted stock awards were granted under the 2011 Stock Incentive Plan at 30% of Ms. Clark&#8217;s base salary and 20% of each other named executive officers&#8217; base salary and are subject to a three-year vesting schedule. These awards were considered transitionary, as the 2025 Stock Incentive Plan was approved by stockholders at the 2025 Annual Meeting. Of the awards issued for 2025, 50% were issued as time-vesting restricted shares under the 2011 Stock Incentive Plan, and 50% were issued as performance-vesting restricted shares under the 2025 Plan. In 2026, restricted stock awards were granted under the 2025 Plan and included 50% time-vesting and 50% performance-vesting restricted shares. The performance vesting shares are contingent on achieving certain financial metrics over a three-year performance period. The financial metrics are Return on Average Assets and Tangible Book Value Growth relative to peers.</p>

<p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>

<p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;text-indent:36pt;"><i><span style="text-decoration: underline; ">2011 Stock Incentive Plan</span></i><i>. </i>The 2011 Stock Incentive Plan, or Plan, was approved by the stockholders on October 20, 2011. The 2011 Plan was amended when approved by the stockholders on April 23, 2015, April 20, 2017, April 23, 2020, and April 21, 2022. When the 2025 Stock Incentive Plan was approved on April 24, 2025, the 2011 Plan was terminated and no additional awards were to be made under the 2011 Plan. Under the 2011 Plan, awards of Eagle&#8217;s common stock could be made to eligible directors, officers and employees. The maximum number of shares available to be awarded was 639,998. Awards available under the Plan included stock options (which includes non-qualified stock options and incentive stock options) and restricted stock. Any shares delivered pursuant to an award could consist, in whole or in part, of authorized but unissued shares or of treasury shares. No stock options were awarded under the Plan. Further, no more than 246,427 shares could be available for awards granted in the form of options. If any shares covered by an award granted under the Plan, or to which such an award relates, were forfeited, or if an award otherwise terminated without the delivery of shares or of other consideration, then the shares covered by such award, or to which such award relates, or the number of shares otherwise counted against the aggregate number of shares available under the Plan with respect to such award, to the extent of any such forfeiture or termination, were again available for granting awards under the Plan.</p>

<p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>

<p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 10pt; font-variant: normal; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt; text-indent: 36pt;"><i><span style="text-decoration: underline; ">2025 Stock Incentive Plan.</span></i><i> </i>The 2025 Stock Incentive Plan, or Plan, was approved by the stockholders on April 24, 2025, to replace the 2011 Plan. Effective that date, the 2011 Plan was terminated and no additional awards were to be made under that Plan. Under the 2025 Plan, awards of Eagle&#8217;s common stock may be made to eligible directors, officers and employees. The maximum number of shares available to be awarded is 257,578, including 82,578 excess shares transferred from the&#160;2011 Plan upon adoption of the 2025 Plan. Awards available under the Plan include stock options (which includes non-qualified stock options and incentive stock options), restricted stock awards or units, performance awards, and substitute awards.&#160;Any shares delivered pursuant to an award may consist, in whole or in part, of authorized but unissued shares or of treasury shares. No stock options have been awarded to date under the Plan. If any shares covered by an award granted under the Plan, or to which such an award relates, are forfeited, or if an award otherwise terminates without the delivery of shares or of other consideration, then the shares covered by such award, or to which such award relates, or the number of shares otherwise counted against the aggregate number of shares available under the Plan with respect to such award, to the extent of any such forfeiture or termination, will again be available for granting awards under the Plan.</p>

<p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>

<div class="PGBK" style="width: 100%; margin-left: 0pt; margin-right: 0pt">
<div class="PGFTR" style="text-align: center; width: 100%">
<div class="hf-row">
<div class="hf-cell PGNUM" style="text-align: center; font-size: 10pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;">- 20 -</div>
</div>
</div>

<hr style="PAGE-BREAK-AFTER: always; border: none; width: 100%; height: 2px; color: #000000; background-color: #000000"/>
<div class="PGHDR" style="text-align: left; width: 100%">
<div class="hf-row">
<div class="hf-cell TOCLink">&#160;</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt; text-align: left">&#160;</p>

<p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;text-indent:36pt;">The purposes of the 2025 Plan are to encourage directors, officers and employees of Eagle to acquire a proprietary interest in the growth and performance of the Company, to create an increased incentive to contribute to the Company&#8217;s future success and performance, thus enhancing the value of the Company for the benefit of its stockholders, and to enhance the ability of the Company and its affiliates to attract and retain highly qualified individuals upon whom, in large measure, the sustained progress, growth and profitability of the Company depends.</p>

<p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>

<table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" class="finTable" style="margin-right: 10%; margin-left: 36pt; width: 90%; font-size: 10pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif; text-indent: 0px;">

		<tbody><tr class="finHeading" style="vertical-align: bottom; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt;">
			<td colspan="8" style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(0, 0, 0); width: 77%;">
			<p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; font-variant: normal; margin: 0pt; text-align: center;"><b>Outstanding Equity Awards at December 31, 2025</b></p>
			</td>
			<td style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; padding-bottom: 1px; width: 1%;">&#160;</td>
		</tr>
		<tr class="finHeading" style="vertical-align: bottom; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt;">
			<td style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; width: 49%;">&#160;</td>
