<p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;text-indent:36pt;"><i><span style="text-decoration: underline; ">Relationship Between </span></i><span style="text-decoration: underline; ">&#8220;</span><i><span style="text-decoration: underline; ">Compensation Actually Paid</span></i><span style="text-decoration: underline; ">&#8221;</span><i><span style="text-decoration: underline; "> and Performance Measures</span></i>. The charts below show, for the past three years, the relationship between the CEO and non-CEO &#8220;compensation actually paid&#8221; and (i) the Company&#8217;s TSR; and (ii) the Company&#8217;s net income.</p>

<p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;text-indent:36pt;">&#160;</p>

